    "CAS_limitation": "Existing provisional piControl mapping affects radiation; inconsistent CAS branch metadata also preclude asserting verified restart continuity. No offsets applied to temperature.",
    "caption": "Figure 3. Global radiative and near-surface air-temperature responses. (a, b) piControl-relative net radiation (black), absorbed shortwave contribution (orange), and negative outgoing-longwave contribution (blue) for the non-recovery and recovery groups. Thin lines show individual models and thick lines show equal-weight group means; all components are plotted as solid lines. (c) Non-recovery minus Recovery group means. Radiation uses two non-recovery models (CESM2 and CNRM-ESM2-1) and three recovery models (CAS-ESM2-0, GFDL-ESM4, and NorESM2-LM). Lines show saved 11-year centred means, computed within each forcing phase; the vertical dotted line marks the forcing reversal. (d, e) Group-mean temperature changes between experiment years 271\u2013280 and 1\u201310, with UKESM1-0-LL also included in the non-recovery temperature group (three models in each group). Cross-hatching marks grid cells where the three model changes do not all have the same sign. (f) Difference between the two group-mean temperature changes (non-recovery minus recovery); cross-hatching marks differences that do not pass a two-sided circular year-block bootstrap test (9,999 resamples; maximum p across block lengths of 2, 3, and 4 years), followed by global Benjamini\u2013Hochberg FDR correction at q < 0.05. The test estimates temporal sampling uncertainty conditional on the six fixed models. Temperature maps use the same colour scale.",
