  "CAS_alignment_limitation": "Not an independently validated branch mapping. Forced parent_time_units declares1850 origin while actual control uses0001; CDR branch dates also conflict with actual coordinates. The relative-start mapping is provisional and calendar200-479 plus all550 alternatives are retained.",
  "caption": "Figure 3. Global radiative and near-surface air-temperature responses. (a, b) piControl-relative net radiation (black), absorbed shortwave contribution (orange), and negative outgoing-longwave contribution (blue) for the non-recovery and recovery groups. Thin solid lines show individual-model shortwave and longwave contributions, using a model-specific hue with darker shades for shortwave and lighter shades for longwave. Thick solid lines show equal-weight group means in (a, b) and their difference in (c), with net, shortwave, and longwave contributions in black, orange, and blue, respectively. Individual-model net radiation is omitted for clarity. (c) Non-recovery minus Recovery group means. Radiation uses two non-recovery models (CESM2 and CNRM-ESM2-1) and three recovery models (CAS-ESM2-0, GFDL-ESM4, and NorESM2-LM). Lines show 11-year centred means computed across the full 280-year sequence; the vertical dotted line marks the forcing reversal. (d, e) Group-mean temperature changes between experiment years 271\u2013280 and 1\u201310, with UKESM1-0-LL also included in the non-recovery temperature group (three models in each group). Cross-hatching marks grid cells where the three model changes do not all have the same sign. (f) Difference between the two group-mean temperature changes (non-recovery minus recovery); cross-hatching marks differences that do not pass a two-sided circular year-block bootstrap test (9,999 resamples; maximum p across block lengths of 2, 3, and 4 years), followed by global Benjamini\u2013Hochberg FDR correction at q < 0.05. The test estimates temporal sampling uncertainty conditional on the six fixed models. Temperature maps use the same colour scale. Stippling marks three-model sign agreement in (d, e) and FDR-significant differences in (f); cross-hatching marks cells failing the respective criterion. Dots are displayed every fourth grid point for clarity. In (d, e), purple and green dashed lines show the initial and final 15% contours of three-model group-mean annual sea-ice concentration in both hemispheres. Magenta solid lines show NOAA/NSIDC observed annual-mean ice edges for 1988\u20132020.",
